This repository is released under two licences, because it contains two
different kinds of work.

  TEXT AND DATA  — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
    Covers the prose of the study, the evidence records, the chain maps, the
    32-object corpus in `data/`, the codebook, and the documents in `docs/`.
    Full legal code: LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt
    Summary: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    CC BY 4.0 is used rather than a software licence because it covers sui
    generis database rights, which a software licence does not, and because it
    states an attribution obligation in terms a reuser of prose and data can act on.

  SOFTWARE  — MIT (full text below)
    Covers the JavaScript, CSS and build/deployment scripts in this repository.

  THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL — not covered by either of the above
    * The Inter typeface embedded in `index.html` is Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter
      Project Authors and is licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
      Full text: third-party/Inter-OFL-1.1.txt
    * Every primary and secondary source cited in the study remains subject to
      its own rights holder. Citations link directly to the source; no third-party
      text is redistributed here beyond short quotation.

Attribution, when reusing the text or data, should name the author, the version,
and link to the work — for example:

  Çandöken, Ahmet (2026). Aktarım Zinciri / The Transmission Chain, v5.3.
  https://ahmet3ddd.github.io/bilginin-tasinma-yolculugu/  — CC BY 4.0

See CITATION.cff for machine-readable citation metadata, and the "Terms of use,
disclaimer and privacy" section inside the study for the conditions that go with
reuse — in particular that the work has not been through human peer review and
was produced with AI assistance, and that both facts should travel with it.

